WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:21.920
[Music]

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:27.060
[Narrator:] For evacuation of the wounded, sleds are used with bipartite skids. A boxlike body, made of wood and cardboard, is erected on them.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:48.300
[Music]

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.800
[Narrator:] Every sled is equipped with a stretcher.

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:59.460
[Music]

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:05.960
[Narrator:] The stretcher is provided with a woolen blanket, paper blankets, and evacuation paper sacks.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:21.280
[Music]

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:28.700
[Narrator:] The sleds are driven this way to the sled-loading place, which is located immediately behind the front line.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:03:20.800
[Music]

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:30.940
[Narrator:] For rescue of the wounded, and for transport from the front line to the sled-loading place, canoe-like sleds are used.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:04:31.940
[Music]

00:04:33.000 --> 00:06:05.000
[Explosions, machine-gun fire, and dramatic music]

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:11.720
[Narrator:] While one medical corpsman applies the first dressing, the other one prepares the evacuation.

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:29.480
He puts an under-blanket of several layers of kraft paper on the bottom of the sled as a separating layer.

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:32.460
and spreads over it the evacuation sack made of kraft paper.

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:57.840
[Music]

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:07.500
[Narrator:] Around the evacuation sack, a layer of tar paper is fastened to increase the insulating effect.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:08:05.160
[Music]

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:14.440
[Narrator:] The hood protects the head against freezing.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:10:15.800
[Music]

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:24.480
[Narrator:] At the sled-loading place, the casualty is transferred to a horse-drawn sled prior to his evacuation.

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:56.560
[Music]

00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:04.200
[Narrator:] As additional protection during the evacuation to the aid station, one or several blankets of crepe paper are used.

00:11:05.560 --> 00:11:37.300
[Music]

00:11:42.100 --> 00:12:04.620
[Shells detonate, followed by lively music]

00:12:04.640 --> 00:12:44.160
[Music]

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:55.000
[Narrator:] A paper bag made of kraft paper protects the wounded arm.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:13:04.860
The bandage of soft crepe paper primarily intended for dressing purposes can also be used in this instance as a sling.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:14:37.780
[Music, punctuated by explosions]

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:47.140
[Narrator:] [Inaudible] is immediately treated by rubbing with snow. The moist skin is then rubbed dry.

00:15:16.780 --> 00:15:22.300
When the canoe-shaped sleds are not available in sufficient number for the evacuation of the wounded,

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:30.140
the medical corpsmen quickly construct auxiliary stretchers by the use of a kraft paper sheet and the wounded man's own skis.

00:15:31.960 --> 00:19:55.440
[Music]

00:19:55.640 --> 00:20:01.140
[Narrator:] The medical corpsmen fasten their own ski sticks to the stretcher in order to have both hands free.

00:20:03.140 --> 00:22:20.300
[Music]

00:22:20.900 --> 00:22:26.020
[Narrator:] In addition to the serious casualties, one or two of the minor wounded are evacuated in the sled.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:43.080
[Music]

00:22:43.620 --> 00:22:51.140
[Narrator:] The aid station, with a squad for medical service, is located a few miles behind the front line.

00:22:51.800 --> 00:24:11.340
[Music]

00:24:12.380 --> 00:24:20.660
[Narrator:] The entrance leads through a windbreak into the interior of the medical service tent, which is heated by two tent stoves.

00:24:20.860 --> 00:24:29.700
A stretcher placed on two wooden blocks is set up as an operating table. A lamp with an incandescent mantle takes care of the lighting.

00:24:30.700 --> 00:24:36.120
[Music]

00:24:36.440 --> 00:24:43.880
[Narrator:] The drinking water is kept in a folding water sack made of rubberized material which is suspended on three poles.

00:24:46.160 --> 00:25:18.260
[Music]

00:25:18.680 --> 00:25:27.080
[Narrator:] The medical officer places a firm parchment-like crepe paper underneath the instruments. The paper has been boiled to sterilize it.

00:25:30.800 --> 00:25:35.600
This sulfide-treated paper can be boiled twenty-one times without tearing.

00:25:42.960 --> 00:25:47.680
Blood-stained or soiled pieces can be washed, dried, and used again.

00:25:49.920 --> 00:26:11.540
[Music]

00:26:12.340 --> 00:26:20.840
[Narrator:] In the case of plaster casts, the medical officer uses a warming dressing made of several layers of crepe paper quilted together and hemmed.

00:26:21.580 --> 00:27:05.760
[Music]

00:27:06.200 --> 00:27:13.420
[Narrator:] A crepe paper cover is rolled around the dressing to prevent bleeding through the bandage, and resultant freezing of the wound.

00:27:17.120 --> 00:27:59.800
[Music]

00:28:00.440 --> 00:28:09.600
[Narrator:] The blood-weakened casualty is carefully protected against any possible danger of freezing. Two or three bags keep the injured leg warm.

00:28:13.040 --> 00:28:51.460
[Music]

00:28:51.800 --> 00:29:01.840
[Narrator:] In case of a more distant evacuation, in place of the evacuation protection sack, a sleeping bag is taken, consisting of several layers of crepe paper.

00:29:02.080 --> 00:29:08.580
This will increase the warmth on account of the insulating effect of the air space between the paper layers.

00:29:10.180 --> 00:30:29.300
[Music]

00:30:35.760 --> 00:30:45.220
[Narrator:] If many stretchers are to be used, the kraft paper sheets and a few thin poles can be most useful in the rapid construction of temporary stretchers and beds.

00:30:47.140 --> 00:30:53.980
The weight resistance of the kraft paper sheet is two-hundred kilograms. That is four-hundred and forty pounds.

00:30:57.180 --> 00:31:06.920
In order to prevent the danger of freezing during evacuation to the distant hospital, some hot water or hot sand-filled bottles are put into the sleeping bags.

00:31:11.680 --> 00:32:24.760
[Music]

